+# Sources consulted
+
+- Title: Upgrade failure for vCenter 8.0 U3j, ESXi 8.0 U3j and NSX 4.2.4 during upgrade to VCF 9.1.0.x
+  Publisher: Broadcom
+  Accessed: 2026-08-14
+  URL: https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/448135/upgrade-failure-for-vcenter-80-u3j-esxi.html
+  Conclusion used: the listed source builds are chronologically later than the VCF 9.1.0 baseline builds, so lifecycle management blocks their direct transition as a back-in-time upgrade.
+
+- Title: Upgrade sequence and related issues for VMware Cloud Foundation 9.1
+  Publisher: Broadcom
+  Accessed: 2026-08-14
+  URL: https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630/upgrade-sequence-and-related-issues-for.html
+  Conclusion used: VCF 9.1 brownfield adoption is topology-sensitive and uses VCF Installer workflows; independent component upgrades are not a supported substitute when NSX is present.
